From b3ba7bd4cc5cd3523881d4d382ba670d64292ac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:35:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ss3ds: wilds sense your lead, seasonal bugs, partner spots
 wilds (0301)

Hook 0110 block v27, gated by Alive wild Pokemon (no new toggle, no new state in P3DS_WildMemV2):
- When a wild one notices the player it sizes up the lead (first healthy non-egg party Pokemon, SS3DS_WildLead in
  encounter_check.c): a lead 25+ levels higher scares it off (15+ half the time; never a shiny), a land one 5+ levels
  above a weaker lead may charge, and one of the same species as the lead comes over curious.
- The flyer slot sometimes sends a bug instead of a bird on routes in clear weather: spring/summer days (Ledyba in the
  morning, Butterfree, Beautifly, Yanma...), Volbeat/Illumise on summer nights, a few in autumn, none in winter. The
  area's own bug flyers first. Bugs fly low, flutter, zigzag, and make no wing-beat sound (birdLow = 2).
- The walking partner shows a "!" over its head when a wild one within 7 tiles notices the player (2 s for a shiny
  spawn) and turns to look when the player stands still. Its size is read once per sighting, not per frame.
Logs: "backs off from your lv", "sizes up your lv", "one of its own kind", "flyer species ... BUG", "your partner spotted".
